Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5), dconf-cli, rsync, gnupg, tar, libsecret-tools, pkexec | policykit-1
Recommends: flatpak, libnotify-bin, rclone
Maintainer: BreizhMann <robi@iactualite.info>
Homepage: https://www.iactualite.info/
Description: Desktop Backup: back up and restore your GNOME desktop
 Sauvegarde du bureau backs up and restores applications (apt, snap, flatpak),
 third-party repositories, GNOME extensions, desktop settings (dconf) and,
 optionally, browser and mail profiles and personal configurations, through a
 GTK4/libadwaita interface in English or French.
 .
 Backups are protected by a SHA-256 checksum, checked when created, before
 restoring and after rotation. They can be encrypted (GPG) and copied to the
 cloud (rclone), restored in full or one file at a time, and compared. A "New
 PC" wizard sets up a new machine step by step. Scheduled backups are rotated
 and re-checked automatically, with a notification if anything goes wrong.
 .
 An optional dry-run restore decrypts and extracts a whole archive into a
 private temporary folder, checks its internal checksums, then deletes
 everything: the only real proof that a backup can be recovered.
